# seed: 1
# requires: shop_buy item_use travel panel_open trophy_bag_resize
# requires-match: panel_open kind=Trophy\ Bag
#
# `item_html` / `item_html_missing` (items.c:205-206) is deliberately NOT asserted here.
# Both fire only on the ITEM_HTML class, and retail Evergreen has exactly three class-201
# items -- 96 "Quest Dictionary", 1024 "Guild Hall", 5119 "Forum" -- all with their arg-4
# page index 0, level 0 and find-probability 0, and no scene in the world GIVEs or OFFERs
# any of them, so no playable hero can ever hold one. That code path is covered instead by
# tests/missions_html.sh, which drives the probe world where such an item is obtainable.
# `panels.kind` was never an EVT either: panels.c:691 emits it through panels_dump into the
# dump file, not the event log, so the assertion above names the panel_open EVT the port
# really does emit.
#
# The item classes end to end, all of them earned in play at the retail Gateway of
# Dreams (Evergreen SCENE 3, quest.txt:1583-1700, the only scene on the main map that
# gives items):
#   * class 0 POTION  - item 1 "Health Potion", 10 GP, bought in the scene's
#     `OFFER2 0,10` shop, then used from the ITEMS panel.
#   * class 4 TRAVEL  - item 99 "Ticket Home", class word "4.0.0.0.1" = mode 0,
#     map 0, link 0, drop in 1. The scene hands it over on the first visit
#     (`IF I99, @skipTicket` / `GIVE I99`), and FUN_0046F60F's guard means the ticket
#     has no scene restriction (travel_scene is the FIFTH dotted component, absent
#     here), so it is used from the map, which is not its destination.
#   * the trophy bag - trophies.txt documents num.TrophyBagWidth/Height as READ/WRITE
#     and the scene sets them to 4x3 on the first visit, which is the only route to
#     FUN_0046FED9 (trophy_bag_resize) in the whole port. The bag is then opened from
#     the ITEMS screen with the bag button (G: Trophies).
# The `1:` and `'` lines are advanced with RETURN, the golden-rule ASK 30 is answered
# with Y (scene.c's ST_ASK: `in->pressed['y']` sets the reply to "YES"), and the shop
# panel is closed with ESCAPE, which panels.c:368 consumes so the scene stays.
expect boot_menu 900
key RETURN
wait 30
key RETURN
wait 30
key RETURN
wait 30
key n
wait 5
text Collector
key RETURN
expect hero_ready 300
expect map_enter 600
keydown DOWN
expect scene_enter 400
keyup DOWN
wait 40
key RETURN
wait 40
key RETURN
wait 40
key RETURN
wait 40
key y
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 40
key RETURN
wait 40
expect panel_open 600
key b
expect shop_buy 200
key ESCAPE
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
